The strongest approach combines the client’s perspective with appropriate professional support. Consultation should strengthen individualized assessment rather than replace direct communication with the client.
Why the Other Answers Are Incorrect
A. Incorrect. The client’s perspective is essential, not inherently unreliable. Excluding the client may lead to misunderstanding and an assessment based on incomplete information.
B. Incorrect. Cultural relevance does not automatically rule out clinical concern. The therapist must still evaluate distress, impairment, safety, context, and meaning.
C. Incorrect. Reaching a diagnosis before adequate assessment may reinforce a premature conclusion and encourage confirmation bias.
CTA Exam Strategy: Consultation should add perspective—not substitute for asking the client.',
