		'option_c'       => 'The therapist’s repeated disregard may reflect incompetence or harmful professional conduct because relevant information is being ignored while the client’s condition worsens',
		'option_d'       => 'The therapist should continue until the client provides written proof that the practices are culturally recognized',
		'correct_option' => 'c',
		'explanation'    => 'C. Correct.
The concern is not simply that the therapist made an initial mistake. The therapist repeatedly ignores clinically relevant information, labels the client without adequate assessment, and continues an ineffective approach despite worsening distress.
This pattern may affect competence, clinical judgment, treatment effectiveness, and client welfare. The therapist should reassess the treatment, explore the client’s perspective, correct unsupported documentation, seek consultation or education, and modify or refer when necessary.
Why the Other Answers Are Incorrect
